course: dictionary
lesson: 7721
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find out which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. The context is the clue. «A puck slides a long way on ice because there is little friction to slow it.» Here, a puck is something that slides on ice, so it must be a thing, not a person or an animal.
explain: «In ice hockey, where players chase a puck, the stick is kept below the shoulders, because a high stick can injure faces.» The words ice hockey and stick tell you that puck means the flat rubber disc used in the game. Always ask: what does the sentence tell me about this word?
explain: The word puck has another meaning too. In Shakespeare's play «A Midsummer Night's Dream», Puck is the name of a mischievous fairy. If a sentence talks about a fairy, a play or a magic trick, that is a clue that the writer means the fairy, not the rubber disc.
fact: A puck is a hard, flat, round rubber disc.
fact: Pucks are used in ice hockey instead of a ball.
fact: Players hit the puck with a hockey stick, and try to get it into the goal.
fact: Puck is also the name of a mischievous fairy in Shakespeare's play «A Midsummer Night's Dream».
fact: Words with more than one meaning are called multiple-meaning words, and the context tells you which meaning is used.
exercise: «A puck slides a long way on ice because there is little friction to slow it.» What is a puck in this sentence? | A fairy who plays tricks on people | *A hard, flat, round rubber disc | A kind of ice cream | A small sled for children
exercise: «In ice hockey, where players chase a puck, the stick is kept below the shoulders, because a high stick can injure faces.» Why must the stick stay below the shoulders? | Because players must hold the stick with one hand | Because the puck is too heavy to lift | *Because a high stick can hurt people's faces | Because the referee likes it that way
exercise: Which words in these phrases are about ice hockey? «hit the puck» and «pass the puck» | Hit and pass mean sleeping and eating | *Hit and pass are things players do with the puck | Hit and pass are names of two fairies | Hit and pass mean crying and laughing
test: «Puck, the mischievous fairy, played tricks on the sleeping lovers in the forest.» What does puck mean here? | *The name of a mischievous fairy | A cold drink from the freezer | A stick used to hit a ball | A flat rubber disc used in hockey
test: «The puck went in, and the crowd cheered.» What does the puck do in this sentence? | It melts on the ice | It is put in a bag | It runs away from the players | *It goes into the goal
exam: «Pass the puck to Maya, she is open near the goal.» What is the best meaning of puck in this sentence? | A kind of ice cream | A small pet dog | *A flat rubber disc used in ice hockey | A fairy from a play by Shakespeare
